{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/646204-vitae-mechanics-questions","id":646204,"title":"Vitae Mechanics questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-30T19:36:34-07:00","id":646204,"title":"Vitae Mechanics questions","content":"Hello, how is everyone tonight.<br /> <br /> I come to ask you guys a question. I went to look at Protean (p140 vtr 2e) third dot beast skin which takes 2 vitae to activate.<br /> I recall there being a rule that you can use only as much vitae as you have BP. I Haven't been able to find this in the book was it taken out for 2nd edition. Or can a 1BP kindred not use beast skin. <br /> <br /> Hope that made sense to you all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T19:47:48-07:00","id":646260,"title":"","content":"In the Blood Potency chart it should show you how many Vitae you can use per turn, I don't recall what it is exactly but it's not a 1:1 with Blood Potency. For larger requirements you can apparently take time to build up the necessary Vitae or whatever energy you're using. It's a rule that's only sporadically been in print, but we had another thread about it.<br /> <br /> The rule is basically this. 'If a power would require she spend more energy than she may in a turn, she can spend the required energy over a number of turns, with the ability activating once she has spent the total needed.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T00:42:20-07:00","id":646422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/646204-vitae-mechanics-questions?p=646260#post646260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Blood Potency chart it should show you how many Vitae you can use per turn, I don't recall what it is exactly but it's not a 1:1 with Blood Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 1:1 in Second Edition. Up to BP 8, anyway. At BP 9 you can spend 10 in a turn, and at BP 10 you can spend 15. But for most practical purposes it may as well be 1:1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/646204-vitae-mechanics-questions?p=646260#post646260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For larger requirements you can apparently take time to build up the necessary Vitae or whatever energy you're using. It's a rule that's only sporadically been in print, but we had another thread about it.<br /> <br /> The rule is basically this. 'If a power would require she spend more energy than she may in a turn, she can spend the required energy over a number of turns, with the ability activating once she has spent the total needed.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. You can always build up over multiple turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T03:18:40-07:00","id":646466,"title":"","content":"Over <i>consecutive</i> turns I might add in case that wasn't clear. So if you can only spend 1 Vitae/turn and you start in turn 1 to activate Beast Skin, then in turn two you are harmed and decided to heal with your Vitae, by turn three you have to start all over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T07:45:17-07:00","id":646653,"title":"","content":"With that specific power you can easily imagine the transformation taking place over two turns instead of one. Instead of your body warping and stretching for 3 seconds, it does it for 6. Same end result. Just takes longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T11:16:57-07:00","id":646981,"title":"","content":"Cool thank you guys for the response. If i could ask for a reference in the book where the build of multiple turns is in the book is cause i'm sure ill have to reference how, or is that a general house ruled thing. <br /> <br /> Also with beast skin the action is instant so can it still be &quot;channeled&quot; or broken up to multiple turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T11:44:18-07:00","id":647021,"title":"","content":"The closest I could find is a reference to the ability to spend vitae over multiple turns for a discipline is in the text of the Juggernaut's Gait devotion, but it's been made clear on here a few times that that is indeed just a regular ability vampires have. If you think about it it makes sense. Vampires don't think in terms of turns. There's just vitae and how long it takes them to spend it to achieve a given result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T11:50:16-07:00","id":647023,"title":"","content":"It is the sort of thing that could use some explicit clarification in the book though. At least if it's supposed to be commonly understood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T11:58:29-07:00","id":647027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/646204-vitae-mechanics-questions?p=647023#post647023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is the sort of thing that could use some explicit clarification in the book though. At least if it's supposed to be commonly understood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I could have sworn it was in the FAQ, but I just looked, and it's not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:49:22-07:00","id":647154,"title":"","content":"What logical explanation can justify the alternative? Vampires can only use vitae towards the same purpose for a few seconds. No, then they can't heal every turn. The limitation is on how much vitae that can be used at one time. A vampire can continuously use vitae up to their limit per turn until the vampire runs out of vitae. I have nothing against it being addressed somewhere, but I don't see how there can be confusion if a person actually thinks about it. I think confusion is based on weak game mechanics found elsewhere with magic points or spells per day. It's artificial representations that came first creating the problem.<br /> <br /> Times are a changing. Get with the program, peeps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T00:18:14-07:00","id":647749,"title":"","content":"This rule is specified in several books and is a general rule among all splats, if you can't power a power in a single turn, you do it in consecutive turns until done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}